From cda4856a13016d817efaca8b2dcc26214b33d37c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pugant <pugant@local>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 15:32:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(spec): concat round MTP(k1) head + DFlash block
 conditioned [t8 stadio 2]

Core mechanism of the T8 stage-2 plan (spec 2026-08-21-t8-stadio2-concat-design
section 3): in a dual draft-mtp + draft-dflash routing armed with
--spec-concat-k1 > 0, a sequence routed to draft-dflash composes its round as
an MTP head of up to k1 tokens followed by the draft-dflash noise block
conditioned on that head - one verify per round on k1 + 7 + 1 columns
(9 with k1=1, 14 with k1=6, within the patched 16-column dmmv cap).

common/speculative.cpp (draft-loop orchestration):
- common_speculative_draft(): for a concat-routed sequence the MTP arm runs
  first with dp.n_max temporarily clamped to k1 (the head cap), the first-wins
  close is skipped for it, and the head tokens are stashed via the new
  common_speculative_draft_params::concat_head (backed by per-seq harness
  storage). The draft-dflash arm consumes the head and closes the round, so
  impl_last still attributes the round to draft-dflash exactly as in the T7
  routing. A failed/empty head (p_min stop or a boundary miss) degrades to a
  plain draft-dflash round - drafting is re-armed because the MTP arm disables
  the sequence on a boundary miss (spec section 10: never a lost round, and
  the boundary warning is demoted to debug for routed sequences, matching the
  neutral-resync precedent in process()).
- draft-dflash draft(): the drafting input carries the head tokens at
  positions n_past+1..n_past+k1' and the noise block shifts to
  n_past+k1'+1..n_past+k1'+n_draft; the anchor (id_last @ n_past) is
  unchanged. dp.result keeps the concatenated draft (single result per seq);
  the n_min/n_max checks are per-SEQ and the shared-result truncate extends
  its cap by the head size. A mid-round decode failure closes a SHORT round
  with the head tokens already drafted (never SRV_ERR, spec section 10).
- Sequences are now decoded in width groups: the DFlash2 selector graph
  requires a uniform per-seq width within one decode (tokens_per_block =
  n_tokens / n_seqs_unq with an exact-division assert), so a batch mixing a
  concat round with a plain block would abort. Each group is sampled right
  after its own decode (the host buffers are overwritten by the next one).

Engine plumbing (two structural findings the plan had to absorb):
- the DFlash2 selector lattice clamped its block to the GGUF dflash.block_size
  (8): a 9-row concat batch made t_h_pre_norm smaller than the batch and the
  post-decode host extraction aborted with tensor-read-out-of-bounds. The cap
  is now the trained block size widened by exactly the concat head width via
  the new llama_context_params::dflash_concat_k1 (set by
  common_context_params_to_llama with the same armed dual-MTP+DFlash guard as
  the server boot marker; inert/0 elsewhere). Removing the clamp entirely
  instead explodes on the wide KV-injection mirror batches at graph_reserve
  (node-pool exhaustion) - hence the parametric cap, kept in sync with the
  graph_max_nodes selector budget. Off-distribution quality past the trained
  width is the declared spec section 9 risk, measured by the stage-A gate.

RS sizing (spec section 5): need_n_rs_seq() covers draft.n_max + k1 when the
concat mode is armed, so a partial rejection in a concat round stays on the
RS fast path instead of silently falling back to the full checkpoint-restore
(lands on the target context only - the server zeroes the draft contexts'
n_rs_seq). n_batch/n_ubatch keep the T7 sizing: a round's 9-14 columns fit
trivially and the spec fixes the sizing inside need_n_rs_seq, not the boot
defaults.

k1 = 0 (default) runs zero new code: every branch is gated on the armed
concat configuration and a null concat_head, verified by diff inspection and
by the bit-identical k1=0-vs-no-flag check in the suite.

Verified with scripts/t8-concat-t1.sh (workspace copy, T7 T1 backbone kept
verbatim + Task 3 boot checks + 15 Task 4 mechanism checks): red run
pre-change (t4-mech-fail.log), green run 41/41 (t4-mech-pass.log). Round
evidence: R-lines at 9 columns with k1=1 (1 MTP + 7 dflash + 1 sampled),
variable 3-9 columns per round (p_min early stop, spec section 5), prosa
rounds unchanged (<= 8 columns, MTP-routed), zero full-checkpoint restores
across 17 partially-rejected rounds (RS fast path). The k1=1-vs-k1=0 greedy
spot-check diverges only at the documented boot-to-boot nondeterminism floor
(prefill mode flip 'The'/'We' reproduced by two k1=0 boots of the identical
code path, and exact-tie token flips with top1-top2 gap 0.000) - the
exact-verify invariant is intact.

